            "duration": "15 mins",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Machine Learning\n\n- Machine Learning (ML) is a subset of Artificial Intelligence.\n- It allows machines to learn from data instead of being explicitly programmed.\n- Systems improve automatically with experience.\n- ML focuses on pattern recognition.\n- It is widely used in modern applications.\n- Forms the core of many AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** YouTube recommending videos based on your watch history.\n\n---\n\n### How Machine Learning Works\n\n- Data is collected from different sources.\n- Algorithms are applied to analyze data.\n- Patterns and relationships are identified.\n- Model is trained using this data.\n- Predictions are made based on learned patterns.\n- Accuracy improves with more data.\n\n> **Example:** Email spam filter learning from past emails.\n\n---\n\n### Types of Machine Learning\n\n- Supervised Learning (with labeled data).\n- Unsupervised Learning (without labeled data).\n- Reinforcement Learning (learning through rewards).\n- Each type serves different purposes.\n- Used in various industries.\n- Helps solve complex problems.\n\n> **Example:** Teaching a model with correct answers (supervised learning).\n\n---\n\n### Applications of Machine Learning\n\n- Recommendation systems.\n- Image and speech recognition.\n- Fraud detection systems.\n- Predictive analysis.\n- Medical diagnosis.\n- Automation systems.\n\n> **Example:** Netflix suggesting movies based on your interest.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Machine Learning\n\n- Learns automatically from data.\n- Improves accuracy over time.\n- Handles large data efficiently.\n- Reduces human effort.\n- Useful in real-time systems.\n- Widely applicable.\n\n> **Example:** Self-learning apps improving user experience.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations of Machine Learning\n\n- Requires large amount of data.\n- Can make wrong predictions.\n- Depends on data quality.\n- Needs proper training.\n- May be complex to implement.\n- Requires computational power.\n\n> **Example:** Wrong recommendations due to incorrect data.",
