            "duration": "15 mins",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Data and Information\n\n- Data and information are important in AI.\n- They are often confused but different.\n- Data is raw facts.\n- Information is processed data.\n- Both are essential for decision-making.\n- AI depends heavily on them.\n\n> **Example:** Numbers in a table vs meaningful report.\n\n---\n\n### What is Data?\n\n- Raw, unprocessed facts and figures.\n- Can be numbers, text, images, or sounds.\n- Has no meaning by itself.\n- Needs processing to be useful.\n- Collected from different sources.\n- Used as input for AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Student marks list without analysis.\n\n---\n\n### What is Information?\n\n- Processed and organized data.\n- Has meaning and context.\n- Helps in decision-making.\n- Easy to understand.\n- Derived from data.\n- Used for insights.\n\n> **Example:** Average marks and performance report.\n\n---\n\n### Key Differences\n\n- Data is raw; information is processed.\n- Data has no meaning; information has meaning.\n- Data is input; information is output.\n- Data is unorganized; information is structured.\n- Both are interconnected.\n- Information depends on data quality.\n\n> **Example:** Raw scores vs grade report.\n\n---\n\n### Role in AI Systems\n\n- Data is used to train AI models.\n- Information is used for decisions.\n- Better data leads to better results.\n- AI converts data into useful insights.\n- Data quality affects AI performance.\n- Continuous data improves AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** AI analyzing customer data for business decisions.\n\n---\n\n### Importance of Data and Information\n\n- Essential for AI development.\n- Helps in accurate predictions.\n- Supports decision-making.\n- Improves system performance.\n- Enables automation.\n- Drives innovation.\n\n> **Example:** Companies using customer data to improve services.",
