            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Arithmetic Operations\n\n- Arithmetic operations are basic mathematical calculations.\n- Used in almost every programming and AI system.\n- Includes addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.\n- Forms foundation of all math problems.\n- Used in daily life calculations.\n- Essential for problem-solving.\n\n> **Example:** Adding prices while shopping.\n\n---\n\n### Addition and Subtraction\n\n- Addition combines values together.\n- Subtraction finds difference between values.\n- Used in counting and comparison.\n- Simple and most common operations.\n- Used in financial calculations.\n- Easy to understand.\n\n> **Example:** 5 + 3 = 8, 10 - 4 = 6\n\n---\n\n### Multiplication and Division\n\n- Multiplication is repeated addition.\n- Division splits values into parts.\n- Used in scaling and sharing.\n- Important in AI calculations.\n- Helps in large computations.\n- Widely used in programming.\n\n> **Example:** 4 × 3 = 12, 12 ÷ 3 = 4\n\n---\n\n### Order of Operations (BODMAS)\n\n- Brackets → Orders → Division → Multiplication → Addition → Subtraction.\n- Determines correct calculation sequence.\n- Prevents wrong answers.\n- Important in programming logic.\n- Ensures accuracy.\n- Used in all math systems.\n\n> **Example:** 2 + 3 × 4 = 14 (not 20)\n\n---\n\n### Arithmetic in Programming\n\n- Used in calculations in code.\n- Helps process numerical data.\n- Important for AI algorithms.\n- Used in formulas and logic.\n- Easy to implement.\n- Core of computation.\n\n> **Example:** total = price + tax in Python\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Shopping bill calculation.\n- Banking transactions.\n- AI data processing.\n- Game scoring systems.\n- Engineering calculations.\n- Daily budgeting.\n\n> **Example:** Calculating total marks in exams.",
