            "duration": "18 mins",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Data\n\n- Data is raw facts and figures.\n- It has no meaning on its own.\n- Data is the foundation of AI systems.\n- It can be collected from many sources.\n- Used for analysis and decision-making.\n- AI systems depend heavily on data.\n\n> **Example:** A list of numbers like 10, 20, 30.\n\n---\n\n### Characteristics of Data\n\n- Raw and unprocessed.\n- Can be numbers, text, images, or audio.\n- Collected from real-world sources.\n- Needs processing to become useful.\n- Can be large or small in size.\n- Basis for information creation.\n\n> **Example:** Student marks list without analysis.\n\n---\n\n### Data vs Information\n\n- Data is raw facts.\n- Information is processed data.\n- Data has no meaning alone.\n- Information has context and meaning.\n- Data is input, information is output.\n- Used in AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** 90, 80, 70 → Average = 80\n\n---\n\n### Importance of Data\n\n- Essential for AI training.\n- Helps in decision-making.\n- Used in predictions.\n- Improves system accuracy.\n- Drives machine learning models.\n- Supports automation.\n\n> **Example:** Netflix using viewing data for recommendations.\n\n---\n\n### Data in AI Systems\n\n- AI learns from data.\n- More data = better performance.\n- Used to train models.\n- Helps find patterns.\n- Improves predictions.\n- Core of AI development.\n\n> **Example:** Self-driving cars using road data.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Examples of Data\n\n- Student marks in exams.\n- Weather readings.\n- Customer purchase records.\n- Social media activity.\n- Medical records.\n- Traffic data.\n\n> **Example:** Mobile app tracking daily steps.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion on Data\n\n- Data is everywhere.\n- It is essential for AI and technology.\n- Needs processing to be useful.\n- Forms base of all digital systems.\n- Helps solve real-world problems.\n- Drives innovation.\n\n> **Example:** Google Maps using location data",
