            "id": "top-ai-4-1-2",
            "title": "Types of Data (Structured/Unstructured)",
            "duration": "18 mins",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Data Types\n\n- Data can be classified into types.\n- Main types: Structured and Unstructured.\n- Helps in organizing information.\n- Important for AI systems.\n- Used in data processing.\n- Each type has different format.\n\n> **Example:** Table vs image data\n\n---\n\n### Structured Data\n\n- Organized in rows and columns.\n- Easy to store and analyze.\n- Found in databases.\n- Clearly defined format.\n- Easy for machines to process.\n- Used in spreadsheets.\n\n> **Example:** Student marks table in Excel\n\n---\n\n### Examples of Structured Data\n\n- Bank records.\n- Employee details.\n- Exam results.\n- Inventory lists.\n- Customer databases.\n- Financial reports.\n\n> **Example:** ATM transaction records\n\n---\n\n### Unstructured Data\n\n- No fixed format or structure.\n- Harder to analyze.\n- Includes multimedia data.\n- Needs AI processing.\n- Very large in volume.\n- Common in real world.\n\n> **Example:** Images, videos, and audio files\n\n---\n\n### Examples of Unstructured Data\n\n- Social media posts.\n- Emails and messages.\n- Videos and images.\n- Voice recordings.\n- Documents and PDFs.\n- Web pages.\n\n> **Example:** WhatsApp voice notes\n\n---\n\n### Structured vs Unstructured Comparison\n\n- Structured: Organized, easy to process.\n- Unstructured: Unorganized, complex.\n- Structured used in databases.\n- Unstructured used in AI/ML.\n- Structured is simpler.\n- Unstructured needs AI tools.\n\n> **Example:** Table vs YouTube video\n\n---\n\n### Importance in AI\n\n- Structured data helps quick analysis.\n- Unstructured data needs AI processing.\n- Both are important in AI systems.\n- Used in machine learning models.\n- Helps improve predictions.\n- Enables real-world applications.\n\n> **Example:** AI analyzing images + text together",
