            "id": "top-ai-5-1-2",
            "title": "Types of ML (Supervised, Unsupervised, Reinforcement)",
            "duration": "18 mins",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Types of Machine Learning\n\n- Machine Learning has three main types.\n- Supervised Learning.\n- Unsupervised Learning.\n- Reinforcement Learning.\n- Each type solves different problems.\n- Used in different AI applications.\n\n> **Example:** Different learning methods like teaching styles.\n\n---\n\n### Supervised Learning\n\n- Uses labeled data (input + output).\n- Model learns from examples.\n- Used for prediction tasks.\n- Most common ML type.\n- Requires training data.\n- Very accurate for known outputs.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting exam results based on past scores.\n\n---\n\n### Supervised Learning Examples\n\n- Email spam detection.\n- Weather prediction.\n- House price prediction.\n- Medical diagnosis.\n- Image classification.\n- Credit scoring systems.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting if student will pass or fail.\n\n---\n\n### Unsupervised Learning\n\n- Works on unlabeled data.\n- Finds hidden patterns.\n- No predefined output.\n- Groups similar data together.\n- Used for clustering.\n- Important in data analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Grouping customers based on buying behavior.\n\n---\n\n### Unsupervised Learning Examples\n\n- Customer segmentation.\n- Market basket analysis.\n- Fraud detection patterns.\n- Data clustering.\n- Document grouping.\n- Social network analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Grouping similar news articles automatically.\n\n---\n\n### Reinforcement Learning\n\n- Learning by trial and error.\n- System gets rewards or penalties.\n- Learns from environment.\n- Used in robotics and games.\n- Improves through feedback.\n- Powerful AI technique.\n\n> **Example:** AI playing chess and improving over time.\n\n---\n\n### Comparison of ML Types\n\n- Supervised: learns from labeled data.\n- Unsupervised: finds hidden patterns.\n- Reinforcement: learns from rewards.\n- Each type has different use cases.\n- All are important in AI.\n- Used together in real systems.\n\n> **Example:** Self-driving car uses all three types.",
