            "content": "### Introduction to PyTorch\n\n- PyTorch is an open-source deep learning framework.\n- Developed by Facebook (Meta).\n- Used for building neural networks.\n- Popular in research and development.\n- Easy to learn and use.\n- Strong support for dynamic models.\n\n> **Example:** Research models for AI experiments.\n\n---\n\n### Why PyTorch is Used\n\n- Simple and Python-friendly.\n- Dynamic computation graphs.\n- Easy debugging process.\n- Flexible model building.\n- Strong research community.\n- Widely used in academia.\n\n> **Example:** Training image classification models.\n\n---\n\n### Key Features of PyTorch\n\n- Dynamic computation graph.\n- GPU acceleration support.\n- Tensor operations.\n- Autograd system for gradients.\n- Easy integration with Python.\n- Modular design.\n\n> **Example:** Real-time AI model training.\n\n---\n\n### PyTorch Workflow\n\n- Define neural network model.\n- Load and preprocess data.\n- Forward pass (prediction).\n- Compute loss.\n- Backpropagation.\n- Optimize model.\n\n> **Example:** Training a chatbot NLP model.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of PyTorch\n\n- Easy to understand code.\n- Flexible architecture.\n- Best for research.\n- Fast debugging.\n- Strong community support.\n- Rapid prototyping.\n\n> **Example:** Developing AI prototypes quickly.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Natural language processing models.\n- Computer vision systems.\n- Research AI models.\n- Chatbots and assistants.\n- Robotics AI systems.\n- Medical AI research.\n\n> **Example:** Meta AI research models.",
