            "duration": "15 mins",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "### Introduction to Spam Detection Model\n\n- Spam detection identifies unwanted messages.\n- Uses AI and machine learning techniques.\n- Common in email systems.\n- Classifies messages as spam or not spam.\n- Important for security.\n- Beginner ML classification project.\n\n> **Example:** Email marked as spam automatically.\n\n---\n\n### How It Works\n\n- Email text is collected.\n- AI analyzes keywords and patterns.\n- Model predicts spam or not spam.\n- Uses trained dataset.\n- Applies classification algorithm.\n- Produces final result.\n\n> **Example:** “Win a prize now” → Spam\n\n---\n\n### Key Techniques Used\n\n- Natural Language Processing (NLP).\n- Naive Bayes classifier.\n- Logistic regression.\n- Feature extraction from text.\n- Tokenization and preprocessing.\n- Machine learning models.\n\n> **Example:** Filtering spam emails in Gmail.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages\n\n- Improves email security.\n- Reduces unwanted messages.\n- Saves user time.\n- Automated filtering system.\n- Works in real-time.\n- Widely used in industry.\n\n> **Example:** Gmail spam filter system.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations\n\n- May misclassify emails.\n- Needs continuous training.\n- Can miss new spam patterns.\n- Depends on dataset quality.\n- False positives possible.\n- Requires updates.\n\n> **Example:** Important email going into spam folder.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Email spam filtering.\n- Messaging app filtering.\n- Social media moderation.\n- Security systems.\n- Fraud message detection.\n- Corporate email protection.\n\n> **Example:** Gmail automatically sorting spam emails.",
