    "content": "### Introduction to Deep Learning\n\n- Deep Learning is a specialized part of Machine Learning.\n- It uses neural networks inspired by the human brain.\n- Designed to handle complex data.\n- Works well with images, audio, and text.\n- Requires large datasets.\n- Used in advanced AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Face recognition systems in smartphones.\n\n---\n\n### Neural Networks Basics\n\n- Made of layers: input, hidden, and output layers.\n- Each layer processes information.\n- Neurons pass data to next layer.\n- Learns patterns through training.\n- Mimics brain structure.\n- Improves with more data.\n\n> **Example:** Recognizing handwritten digits.\n\n---\n\n### How Deep Learning Works\n\n- Large datasets are fed into the model.\n- Multiple layers process the data.\n- Features are extracted automatically.\n- Model learns complex patterns.\n- Produces accurate outputs.\n- Improves through training cycles.\n\n> **Example:** AI identifying objects in images.\n\n---\n\n### Applications of Deep Learning\n\n- Image recognition.\n- Speech recognition.\n- Natural language processing.\n- Self-driving cars.\n- Medical diagnosis.\n- AI assistants.\n\n> **Example:** Google Photos recognizing people in pictures.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Deep Learning\n\n- Handles complex data efficiently.\n- High accuracy in predictions.\n- Automatic feature extraction.\n- Improves with large datasets.\n- Useful in advanced AI tasks.\n- Reduces manual effort.\n\n> **Example:** AI translating languages automatically.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations of Deep Learning\n\n- Requires huge data and computing power.\n- Takes longer training time.\n- Difficult to understand (black box).\n- Expensive to implement.\n- Needs specialized hardware.\n- Not suitable for small data tasks.\n\n> **Example:** Training AI models needing powerful GPUs.",
