    "id": "top-ai-2-1-1",
    "title": "What is Programming?",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Programming\n\n- Programming is the process of giving instructions to a computer.\n- These instructions tell the computer what to do step by step.\n- Computers cannot think on their own.\n- They only follow commands written by humans.\n- Programming is the foundation of software and apps.\n- It is essential for building AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Writing code to display “Hello World” on screen.\n\n---\n\n### What is a Program?\n\n- A program is a set of instructions written in a programming language.\n- It performs a specific task.\n- Programs can be simple or complex.\n- They are written by programmers.\n- Each program solves a problem.\n- Programs run on computers and devices.\n\n> **Example:** A calculator app performing addition and subtraction.\n\n---\n\n### Programming Languages\n\n- Languages used to write programs.\n- Examples include Python, Java, and C++.\n- Each language has its own rules (syntax).\n- Some are easier for beginners.\n- Used for different purposes.\n- Help humans communicate with computers.\n\n> **Example:** Python used for AI development.\n\n---\n\n### Why Learn Programming?\n\n- Helps solve real-world problems.\n- Builds logical thinking skills.\n- Enables creation of apps and software.\n- Essential for AI and technology fields.\n- High demand in job market.\n- Improves problem-solving ability.\n\n> **Example:** Creating a simple student record system.\n\n---\n\n### Basic Programming Concepts\n\n- Variables store data.\n- Conditions make decisions.\n- Loops repeat tasks.\n- Functions organize code.\n- Input and output handle user interaction.\n- Logic controls program flow.\n\n> **Example:** Using a loop to print numbers from 1 to 10.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications of Programming\n\n- Mobile apps and games.\n- Websites and online systems.\n- Banking and financial software.\n- AI and automation systems.\n- Embedded systems in devices.\n- Scientific and research tools.\n\n> **Example:** ATM machine software processing transactions.",
