    "id": "top-ai-2-1-2",
    "title": "Algorithms and Flowcharts",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Algorithms\n\n- An algorithm is a step-by-step solution to a problem.\n- It defines a clear sequence of actions.\n- Used before writing actual code.\n- Helps in planning and understanding logic.\n- Makes problem-solving easier.\n- Used in all programming tasks.\n\n> **Example:** Steps to make tea (boil water, add tea, etc.).\n\n---\n\n### Characteristics of Algorithms\n\n- Clear and unambiguous steps.\n- Finite number of steps.\n- Input and output defined.\n- Efficient and logical.\n- Easy to understand.\n- Solves a specific problem.\n\n> **Example:** Algorithm to add two numbers.\n\n---\n\n### Introduction to Flowcharts\n\n- Flowcharts are visual representations of algorithms.\n- Use symbols to show steps.\n- Help understand program flow easily.\n- Useful for beginners.\n- Show sequence and decisions clearly.\n- Improve problem visualization.\n\n> **Example:** Diagram showing steps of login process.\n\n---\n\n### Common Flowchart Symbols\n\n- Oval = Start/End\n- Rectangle = Process\n- Diamond = Decision\n- Arrow = Flow direction\n- Parallelogram = Input/Output\n- Each symbol has a specific role.\n\n> **Example:** Diamond used for “Yes/No” decision.\n\n---\n\n### Benefits of Algorithms and Flowcharts\n\n- Improve clarity of solution.\n- Help in debugging errors.\n- Make coding easier.\n- Save time during development.\n- Improve communication between developers.\n- Useful in planning complex systems.\n\n> **Example:** Planning a game before coding it.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Use of Algorithms\n\n- Used in daily tasks and systems.\n- Found in search engines and apps.\n- Helps automate decisions.\n- Improves efficiency.\n- Used in AI systems.\n- Important in computer science.\n\n> **Example:** Google search algorithm ranking results.",
