    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Logic Building\n\n- Logic building is the ability to think step by step.\n- It helps in solving problems effectively.\n- Important for programming and AI.\n- Focuses on reasoning and decision-making.\n- Improves analytical skills.\n- Foundation of coding.\n\n> **Example:** Deciding steps to solve a math problem.\n\n---\n\n### Why Logic Building is Important\n\n- Helps write correct programs.\n- Reduces errors in code.\n- Improves problem-solving ability.\n- Makes coding easier.\n- Enhances thinking skills.\n- Essential for developers.\n\n> **Example:** Breaking a problem into smaller parts.\n\n---\n\n### Steps in Logic Building\n\n- Understand the problem clearly.\n- Break it into smaller steps.\n- Identify inputs and outputs.\n- Plan solution logically.\n- Test and improve solution.\n- Apply step-by-step thinking.\n\n> **Example:** Solving a calculation step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Use of Conditions (If-Else)\n\n- Helps make decisions in programs.\n- Executes different actions based on condition.\n- Important for control flow.\n- Used in real-world applications.\n- Makes programs dynamic.\n- Easy to implement.\n\n> **Example:** If marks ≥ 50 → Pass, else → Fail.\n\n---\n\n### Use of Loops\n\n- Repeats a task multiple times.\n- Saves time and effort.\n- Used for repetitive operations.\n- Types include for-loop and while-loop.\n- Improves efficiency.\n- Reduces code length.\n\n> **Example:** Printing numbers from 1 to 10 using loop.\n\n---\n\n### Improving Logic Skills\n\n- Practice problem-solving daily.\n- Solve puzzles and exercises.\n- Learn from examples.\n- Write simple programs.\n- Analyze different solutions.\n- Keep improving step by step.\n\n> **Example:** Solving logical puzzles like number patterns.",
