    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### What is Python?\n\n- Python is a high-level programming language.\n- It is easy to learn and use.\n- Widely used in AI, data science, and web development.\n- Has simple and readable syntax.\n- Supports multiple programming styles.\n- Popular among beginners and professionals.\n\n> **Example:** print(\"Hello World\") displays text on screen.\n\n---\n\n### Why Python for AI?\n\n- Simple and easy syntax.\n- Large number of AI libraries.\n- Strong community support.\n- Works well with data.\n- Fast development time.\n- Used in real-world AI projects.\n\n> **Example:** Python used in recommendation systems.\n\n---\n\n### Features of Python\n\n- Easy to read and write.\n- Interpreted language (no compilation needed).\n- Cross-platform (runs on many systems).\n- Large standard library.\n- Supports object-oriented programming.\n- Open-source and free.\n\n> **Example:** Same Python code runs on Windows and Linux.\n\n---\n\n### Basic Syntax of Python\n\n- Code is written line by line.\n- Indentation is important.\n- No need for semicolons.\n- Uses simple keywords.\n- Easy structure for beginners.\n- Code is readable.\n\n> **Example:**\n- if True:\n- print(\"Yes\")\n\n---\n\n### Python in Real Life\n\n- Used in AI and Machine Learning.\n- Web development (websites).\n- Automation scripts.\n- Game development.\n- Data analysis.\n- Scientific computing.\n\n> **Example:** Python used in YouTube recommendation system.\n\n---\n\n### Installing and Running Python\n\n- Download Python from official website.\n- Install on your system.\n- Use IDLE or code editor.\n- Write and run programs.\n- Use terminal or IDE.\n- Practice simple programs.\n\n> **Example:** Running a program that prints your name.",
