    "id": "top-ai-2-2-3",
    "title": "Input/Output Operations",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Input/Output\n\n- Programs interact with users using input and output.\n- Input means taking data from user.\n- Output means displaying result.\n- Essential for interactive programs.\n- Makes programs useful.\n- Used in all applications.\n\n> **Example:** Asking user for name and showing greeting.\n\n---\n\n### Taking Input from User\n\n- Use input() function.\n- Stores user data in variable.\n- Always returns string.\n- Can convert to other types.\n- Used in interactive programs.\n- Simple and effective.\n\n> **Example:** name = input(\"Enter name: \")\n\n---\n\n### Displaying Output\n\n- Use print() function.\n- Shows result on screen.\n- Can display text and variables.\n- Supports multiple values.\n- Easy to use.\n- Important for results.\n\n> **Example:** print(\"Hello\", name)\n\n---\n\n### Formatting Output\n\n- Use f-strings for formatting.\n- Makes output clear.\n- Combine text and variables.\n- Improves readability.\n- Modern Python method.\n- Easy syntax.\n\n> **Example:** print(f\"Age is {age}\")\n\n---\n\n### Type Conversion in Input\n\n- Convert input to required type.\n- Prevents errors in calculations.\n- Use int(), float().\n- Important in numeric input.\n- Ensures correct operations.\n- Common beginner step.\n\n> **Example:** age = int(input(\"Enter age: \"))\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Input/Output Use\n\n- Forms and login systems.\n- ATM machines.\n- Online applications.\n- Games and quizzes.\n- Data entry systems.\n- AI chatbots.\n\n> **Example:** Entering PIN and getting balance info.",
