    "id": "top-ai-2-2-4",
    "title": "Operators",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Operators\n\n- Operators perform operations on data.\n- Used in calculations and logic.\n- Essential in programming.\n- Work with variables and values.\n- Different types available.\n- Simplify coding tasks.\n\n> **Example:** 5 + 3 gives 8.\n\n---\n\n### Arithmetic Operators\n\n- + Addition\n- Subtraction\n- * Multiplication\n- / Division\n- % Modulus\n- ** Power\n\n> **Example:** 10 % 3 gives remainder 1.\n\n---\n\n### Comparison Operators\n\n- == Equal\n- != Not equal\n- > Greater than\n- < Less than\n- >= Greater or equal\n- <= Less or equal\n\n> **Example:** 5 > 3 gives True.\n\n---\n\n### Logical Operators\n\n- and (both conditions true)\n- or (any condition true)\n- not (reverse condition)\n- Used in decision-making.\n- Combine multiple conditions.\n- Important in control flow.\n\n> **Example:** age > 18 and age < 60\n\n---\n\n### Assignment Operators\n\n- = Assign value\n- += Add and assign\n- = Subtract and assign\n- *= Multiply and assign\n- Simplifies code.\n- Saves time.\n\n> **Example:** x += 5 means x = x + 5.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Use of Operators\n\n- Used in calculations.\n- Decision-making in programs.\n- Used in conditions and loops.\n- Important in AI logic.\n- Helps automate tasks.\n- Core part of coding.\n\n> **Example:** Checking if user is eligible (age ≥ 18).",
