    "id": "top-ai-2-3-1",
    "title": "Conditional Statements (if/else)",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Conditional Statements\n\n- Conditional statements are used to make decisions in programs.\n- They allow the program to choose different actions based on conditions.\n- Help create dynamic and interactive programs.\n- Based on True or False logic.\n- Essential for control flow.\n- Used in almost every program.\n\n> **Example:** Checking if a number is positive or negative.\n\n---\n\n### if Statement\n\n- Executes code only if condition is True.\n- Simplest decision-making statement.\n- Improves program logic.\n- Easy to understand.\n- Used for basic checks.\n- Common in programs.\n\n> **Example:**\n- age = 18\n- if age >= 18:\n- print(\"Adult\")\n\n---\n\n### if-else Statement\n\n- Provides two possible outcomes.\n- Executes one block if condition is True.\n- Executes another if False.\n- Useful for decision making.\n- Improves program flexibility.\n- Easy structure.\n\n> **Example:**\n- if marks >= 50:\n- print(\"Pass\")\n- else:\n- print(\"Fail\")\n\n---\n\n### elif (Multiple Conditions)\n\n- Used for multiple conditions.\n- Checks conditions one by one.\n- Executes first True block.\n- Avoids multiple nested ifs.\n- Makes code cleaner.\n- Useful in grading systems.\n\n> **Example:**\n- if marks >= 80:\n- print(\"A\")\n- elif marks >= 50:\n- print(\"B\")\n- else:\n- print(\"C\")\n\n---\n\n### Nested Conditions\n\n- One condition inside another.\n- Used for complex decisions.\n- Improves logical depth.\n- Must be used carefully.\n- Can increase complexity.\n- Helps solve real-world problems.\n\n> **Example:**\n- if age >= 18:\n- if age < 60:\n- print(\"Working Age\")\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Use of Conditions\n\n- Used in login systems.\n- ATM and banking systems.\n- Game decision-making.\n- AI decision processes.\n- User input validation.\n- Automation systems.\n\n> **Example:** Checking username and password before login.",
