    "title": "Matrix Operations",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Matrix Operations\n\n- Matrix operations are ways to manipulate matrices.\n- Used in AI and data processing.\n- Include addition, subtraction, multiplication.\n- Help in solving complex problems.\n- Important in linear algebra.\n- Used in algorithms.\n\n> **Example:** Combining two datasets in AI.\n\n---\n\n### Matrix Addition & Subtraction\n\n- Add/subtract corresponding elements.\n- Matrices must be of same size.\n- Simple element-wise operation.\n- Used in data comparison.\n- Easy to compute.\n- Important in AI models.\n\n> **Example:** Adding two 2×2 matrices of scores.\n\n---\n\n### Matrix Multiplication\n\n- Rows of first × columns of second.\n- Not commutative (A×B ≠ B×A).\n- Used in transformations.\n- Important in neural networks.\n- More complex than addition.\n- Core AI operation.\n\n> **Example:** Image transformation in AI models.\n\n---\n\n### Transpose of Matrix\n\n- Swap rows into columns.\n- Important transformation operation.\n- Used in data restructuring.\n- Helps in calculations.\n- Common in AI systems.\n- Easy to perform.\n\n> **Example:** Converting row data into column format.\n\n---\n\n### Determinant (Basic Idea)\n\n- A value derived from a square matrix.\n- Helps understand matrix properties.\n- Used in solving equations.\n- Important in linear algebra.\n- Used in transformations.\n- Advanced AI concept.\n\n> **Example:** Checking system solvability using determinant.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Use of Matrix Operations\n\n- AI model training.\n- Image processing systems.\n- Robotics movement calculations.\n- 3D graphics rendering.\n- Data science applications.\n- Engineering simulations.\n\n> **Example:** Self-driving cars processing sensor data.",
