    "id": "top-ai-3-3-1",
    "title": "Mean, Median, Mode",
    "duration": "20 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Central Tendency\n\n- Mean, Median, and Mode are measures of central tendency.\n- They help summarize data with a single value.\n- Widely used in statistics and AI.\n- Useful for understanding datasets.\n- Helps in decision-making.\n- Found in real-world data analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Average marks of students in a class.\n\n---\n\n### Mean (Average)\n\n- Mean is the sum of values divided by total count.\n- Shows overall average of data.\n- Sensitive to extreme values.\n- Most commonly used measure.\n- Easy to calculate.\n- Used in AI datasets.\n\n> **Example:** (10+20+30)/3 = 20\n\n---\n\n### Mean in Real Life\n\n- Used in exam results.\n- Used in weather temperature analysis.\n- Helps in business forecasting.\n- Used in AI predictions.\n- Simple and effective.\n- Common in daily life.\n\n> **Example:** Average monthly salary calculation.\n\n---\n\n### Median (Middle Value)\n\n- Median is the middle value in ordered data.\n- Used when data is skewed.\n- Not affected by extreme values.\n- Requires sorting data first.\n- Important in statistics.\n- Used in income analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Median of 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 is 6\n\n---\n\n### Median in Real Life\n\n- Used in income studies.\n- Property price analysis.\n- Exam score distribution.\n- AI data balancing.\n- More reliable in skewed data.\n- Helps avoid distortion.\n\n> **Example:** Median house price in a city\n\n---\n\n### Mode (Most Frequent Value)\n\n- Mode is the most repeated value.\n- A dataset can have one or more modes.\n- Useful for categorical data.\n- Easy to identify.\n- Used in pattern detection.\n- Important in AI classification.\n\n> **Example:** Most common shoe size sold\n\n---\n\n### Comparison of Mean, Median, Mode\n\n- Mean = average value.\n- Median = middle value.\n- Mode = most frequent value.\n- Each used in different situations.\n- Mean sensitive to outliers.\n- Median better for skewed data.\n\n> **Example:** Income analysis using all three measures\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Use in AI\n\n- Data preprocessing in AI models.\n- Removing noise from datasets.\n- Understanding user behavior.\n- Improving prediction accuracy.\n- Statistical analysis in ML.\n- Business intelligence systems.\n\n> **Example:** Netflix analyzing average watch time",
