    "duration": "18 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Data Transformation\n\n- Data transformation is converting data into a useful format.\n- Helps in making data suitable for analysis.\n- Changes structure or format of data.\n- Improves compatibility with AI models.\n- Important preprocessing step.\n- Used in all data systems.\n\n> **Example:** Converting text data into numbers.\n\n---\n\n### Why Data Transformation is Needed\n\n- Raw data is often not usable directly.\n- Makes data easier to analyze.\n- Improves AI model understanding.\n- Ensures consistency.\n- Helps in better predictions.\n- Required for machine learning.\n\n> **Example:** Converting “Yes/No” into 1/0.\n\n---\n\n### Types of Data Transformation\n\n- Normalization (scaling data).\n- Encoding (text to numbers).\n- Aggregation (summarizing data).\n- Smoothing (removing noise).\n- Generalization (simplifying data).\n- Discretization (grouping values).\n\n> **Example:** Scaling marks from 0–100 into 0–1 range.\n\n---\n\n### Data Normalization\n\n- Converts data into same scale.\n- Prevents bias in AI models.\n- Improves learning performance.\n- Common in machine learning.\n- Makes comparison easier.\n- Used in datasets with different ranges.\n\n> **Example:** Converting income values into 0–1 scale.\n\n---\n\n### Data Encoding\n\n- Converts categories into numbers.\n- Required for AI processing.\n- Helps machine understanding.\n- Common in classification tasks.\n- Simplifies input data.\n- Widely used in ML.\n\n> **Example:** Male = 1, Female = 0\n\n---\n\n### Data Transformation in AI\n\n- Prepares data for training.\n- Improves model accuracy.\n- Makes data machine-readable.\n- Essential preprocessing step.\n- Used in all AI pipelines.\n- Enhances performance.\n\n> **Example:** Converting text reviews into sentiment scores.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Banking systems risk analysis.\n- Healthcare data processing.\n- E-commerce recommendation systems.\n- AI chatbots.\n- Weather forecasting systems.\n- Business analytics.\n\n> **Example:** Transforming sales data for forecasting trends.",
