    "id": "top-ai-4-2-3",
    "title": "Handling Missing Data",
    "duration": "18 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Missing Data\n\n- Missing data means incomplete information.\n- Common problem in real datasets.\n- Can affect AI accuracy.\n- Needs proper handling.\n- Occurs due to errors or omissions.\n- Important in data preprocessing.\n\n> **Example:** Student marks missing in a record.\n\n---\n\n### Why Missing Data Happens\n\n- Human error in data entry.\n- System failures.\n- Incomplete surveys.\n- Sensor malfunction.\n- Data loss during transfer.\n- Optional fields not filled.\n\n> **Example:** User skipping age field in form.\n\n---\n\n### Types of Missing Data\n\n- Missing completely at random.\n- Missing at random.\n- Missing not at random.\n- Each type affects analysis differently.\n- Requires different handling methods.\n- Important in statistics.\n\n> **Example:** Missing salary data in survey responses.\n\n---\n\n### Methods to Handle Missing Data\n\n- Removing missing entries.\n- Filling with mean/median/mode.\n- Predicting missing values.\n- Using default values.\n- Data interpolation.\n- Advanced AI estimation methods.\n\n> **Example:** Replacing missing marks with class average.\n\n---\n\n### Impact on AI Models\n\n- Missing data reduces accuracy.\n- Can create bias in models.\n- Affects predictions.\n- Needs preprocessing.\n- Improves model reliability when handled.\n- Important in training phase.\n\n> **Example:** Incomplete customer data affecting recommendations.\n\n---\n\n### Tools for Handling Missing Data\n\n- Python Pandas library.\n- Excel functions.\n- Machine learning libraries.\n- Data preprocessing tools.\n- AI frameworks.\n- Statistical software.\n\n> **Example:** Using Pandas fillna() function.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Healthcare patient records.\n- Banking transaction systems.\n- E-commerce customer data.\n- AI prediction systems.\n- Government databases.\n- Business analytics.\n\n> **Example:** Filling missing medical test results for diagnosis.",
