    "title": "Charts and Graphs",
    "duration": "18 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Data Visualization\n\n- Data visualization means representing data in graphical form.\n- Helps understand complex data easily.\n- Makes patterns and trends visible.\n- Important in AI and data science.\n- Used in reports and analysis.\n- Improves decision-making.\n\n> **Example:** Showing exam marks using a bar chart.\n\n---\n\n### Why Charts and Graphs are Important\n\n- Make data easy to understand.\n- Help compare values quickly.\n- Show trends and patterns.\n- Improve communication of data.\n- Used in business and AI.\n- Save time in analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Sales growth shown in a line graph.\n\n---\n\n### Types of Charts\n\n- Bar chart (comparison).\n- Line chart (trends over time).\n- Pie chart (percentage distribution).\n- Histogram (frequency distribution).\n- Scatter plot (relationship between variables).\n- Each serves different purpose.\n\n> **Example:** Pie chart showing class attendance percentage.\n\n---\n\n### Bar Charts\n\n- Used to compare categories.\n- Easy to interpret.\n- Shows differences clearly.\n- Can be vertical or horizontal.\n- Common in reports.\n- Widely used in AI dashboards.\n\n> **Example:** Comparing marks of students in class.\n\n---\n\n### Line Graphs\n\n- Shows trends over time.\n- Data points connected with lines.\n- Useful for forecasting.\n- Common in AI predictions.\n- Easy to understand growth patterns.\n- Used in analytics.\n\n> **Example:** Temperature changes over a week.\n\n---\n\n### Pie Charts & Histograms\n\n- Pie chart shows parts of a whole.\n- Histogram shows data distribution.\n- Helps in percentage analysis.\n- Used in statistics.\n- Important in AI preprocessing.\n- Simple visual tools.\n\n> **Example:** Pie chart of mobile brand usage.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Business performance reports.\n- AI data dashboards.\n- Weather forecasting charts.\n- Social media analytics.\n- Education performance tracking.\n- Healthcare statistics.\n\n> **Example:** Monthly sales report visualization.",
