    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Data Interpretation\n\n- Data interpretation means understanding visual data.\n- Helps extract meaning from charts.\n- Important in AI and analytics.\n- Converts visuals into insights.\n- Used in decision-making.\n- Core skill in data science.\n\n> **Example:** Understanding sales trend from graph.\n\n---\n\n### Reading Graphs Correctly\n\n- Identify axes and labels.\n- Understand scale values.\n- Look for trends and patterns.\n- Compare data points.\n- Avoid misinterpretation.\n- Important analytical skill.\n\n> **Example:** Reading highest point in line graph.\n\n---\n\n### Finding Trends\n\n- Increasing or decreasing patterns.\n- Helps predict future values.\n- Used in forecasting.\n- Important in AI models.\n- Easy to visualize in graphs.\n- Used in business analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Sales increasing every month.\n\n---\n\n### Comparing Data\n\n- Compare multiple datasets.\n- Identify differences and similarities.\n- Helps in decision-making.\n- Used in reports.\n- Important in AI insights.\n- Improves understanding.\n\n> **Example:** Comparing two product sales charts.\n\n---\n\n### Drawing Conclusions\n\n- Based on visual data.\n- Helps make decisions.\n- Used in AI predictions.\n- Requires logical thinking.\n- Important in analytics.\n- Supports business strategy.\n\n> **Example:** Choosing best-selling product.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Business intelligence reports.\n- Healthcare data analysis.\n- AI model evaluation.\n- Marketing insights.\n- Education performance tracking.\n- Financial forecasting.\n\n> **Example:** Company deciding next product based on graphs.",
