    "id": "top-ai-5-1-1",
    "title": "What is Machine Learning?",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Machine Learning (ML)\n\n- Machine Learning is a branch of Artificial Intelligence.\n- It allows computers to learn from data.\n- No explicit programming for every task.\n- Systems improve with experience.\n- Used in prediction and decision-making.\n- Core part of modern AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Email spam detection system learning from past emails.\n\n---\n\n### How Machine Learning Works\n\n- Data is collected from real world.\n- Algorithm analyzes patterns.\n- Model is trained on data.\n- Predictions are made using model.\n- Performance improves over time.\n- Feedback is used for learning.\n\n> **Example:** Netflix recommending movies based on watch history.\n\n---\n\n### Traditional Programming vs ML\n\n- Traditional: Rules are written manually.\n- ML: System learns rules from data.\n- Traditional is static.\n- ML is adaptive.\n- ML handles complex problems better.\n- Used in real-world AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Spam filter vs rule-based email filter.\n\n---\n\n### Importance of Machine Learning\n\n- Handles large datasets easily.\n- Automates decision-making.\n- Improves accuracy over time.\n- Reduces human effort.\n- Used in many industries.\n- Core of modern AI applications.\n\n> **Example:** Google Maps predicting traffic.\n\n---\n\n### Applications of Machine Learning\n\n- Recommendation systems.\n- Voice assistants.\n- Image recognition.\n- Fraud detection.\n- Medical diagnosis.\n- Self-driving cars.\n\n> **Example:** YouTube suggesting videos.\n\n---\n\n### Machine Learning in AI\n\n- ML is the backbone of AI.\n- Helps systems learn patterns.\n- Used in prediction models.\n- Improves automation.\n- Works with big data.\n- Essential for intelligent systems.\n\n> **Example:** AI chatbot improving responses over time.",
