    "title": "Regression",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Regression\n\n- Regression is a supervised learning technique.\n- It predicts continuous numerical values.\n- Based on input data and trends.\n- Used for forecasting problems.\n- Helps in decision-making.\n- Important in AI and data science.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting house prices.\n\n---\n\n### How Regression Works\n\n- Model learns relationship between variables.\n- Uses historical data.\n- Finds best-fit line.\n- Predicts future values.\n- Works with continuous data.\n- Improves with more data.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting salary based on experience.\n\n---\n\n### Types of Regression\n\n- Linear regression.\n- Multiple regression.\n- Polynomial regression.\n- Each used for different patterns.\n- Helps in modeling relationships.\n- Used in AI predictions.\n\n> **Example:** Sales prediction over time.\n\n---\n\n### Regression in AI\n\n- Used in predictive analytics.\n- Helps in forecasting trends.\n- Used in finance and business.\n- Core ML technique.\n- Works with large datasets.\n- Important for decision systems.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting stock market prices.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Weather forecasting.\n- Salary prediction.\n- House price estimation.\n- Sales forecasting.\n- Medical risk prediction.\n- Economic analysis.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting future electricity demand.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Regression\n\n- Simple and powerful.\n- Easy to interpret.\n- Works with numerical data.\n- Useful in many fields.\n- Provides trend insights.\n- Widely used in AI.\n\n> **Example:** Predicting student performance scores.",
