    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Classification\n\n- Classification is supervised learning.\n- Used to assign categories.\n- Output is discrete (labels).\n- Based on training data.\n- Very common in AI systems.\n- Used in decision-making.\n\n> **Example:** Email spam or not spam.\n\n---\n\n### How Classification Works\n\n- Model learns from labeled data.\n- Finds patterns in features.\n- Assigns class labels.\n- Works with categories.\n- Improves with training.\n- Used in prediction systems.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting disease type from symptoms.\n\n---\n\n### Types of Classification\n\n- Binary classification (two classes).\n- Multi-class classification.\n- Multi-label classification.\n- Each type solves different problems.\n- Used in AI models.\n- Important in decision systems.\n\n> **Example:** Yes/No prediction system.\n\n---\n\n### Classification in AI\n\n- Used in image recognition.\n- Spam detection systems.\n- Medical diagnosis.\n- Sentiment analysis.\n- Fraud detection.\n- Security systems.\n\n> **Example:** Face recognition in smartphones.\n\n---\n\n### Algorithms Used\n\n- Decision Trees.\n- K-Nearest Neighbors.\n- Logistic Regression.\n- Support Vector Machines.\n- Neural Networks.\n- Widely used in AI.\n\n> **Example:** Classifying emails using ML model.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Bank loan approval.\n- Spam filtering.\n- Disease detection.\n- Image classification.\n- Customer segmentation.\n- Fraud detection.\n\n> **Example:** Sorting emails into inbox or spam.",
