    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Training & Testing Data\n\n- Data is divided into training and testing sets.\n- Training data is used to teach the model.\n- Testing data is used to evaluate performance.\n- Important in machine learning.\n- Ensures model accuracy.\n- Prevents overfitting.\n\n> **Example:** 80% training, 20% testing data split.\n\n---\n\n### Training Data\n\n- Used to train the model.\n- Contains input and output data.\n- Helps model learn patterns.\n- Larger portion of dataset.\n- Essential for learning process.\n- Improves model accuracy.\n\n> **Example:** Past student exam results.\n\n---\n\n### Testing Data\n\n- Used to test model performance.\n- Not seen during training.\n- Checks accuracy of predictions.\n- Ensures generalization.\n- Helps detect errors.\n- Very important in AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** New exam results for prediction testing.\n\n---\n\n### Train-Test Split\n\n- Common split: 70-30 or 80-20.\n- Ensures balanced evaluation.\n- Avoids overfitting.\n- Improves model reliability.\n- Standard practice in ML.\n- Used in all AI projects.\n\n> **Example:** 80% training, 20% testing dataset.\n\n---\n\n### Importance in AI\n\n- Ensures model fairness.\n- Improves prediction accuracy.\n- Helps evaluate performance.\n- Prevents memorization.\n- Essential ML step.\n- Used in all models.\n\n> **Example:** Testing chatbot responses with unseen data.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Medical diagnosis systems.\n- Fraud detection models.\n- Recommendation systems.\n- Image recognition AI.\n- Voice assistants.\n- Predictive analytics.\n\n> **Example:** Testing self-driving car model safety.",
