    "title": "Dimensionality Reduction",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Dimensionality Reduction\n\n- Reduces number of input variables.\n- Keeps important information only.\n- Simplifies complex datasets.\n- Improves model performance.\n- Used in data preprocessing.\n- Important in AI and ML.\n\n> **Example:** Reducing 100 features to 10 important ones.\n\n---\n\n### Why Dimensionality Reduction is Needed\n\n- Reduces computation time.\n- Removes irrelevant data.\n- Avoids overfitting.\n- Improves model accuracy.\n- Makes visualization easier.\n- Used in big data systems.\n\n> **Example:** Simplifying student dataset features.\n\n---\n\n### Techniques of Reduction\n\n- Principal Component Analysis (PCA).\n- Feature selection.\n- Linear Discriminant Analysis.\n- t-SNE visualization.\n- Each method has purpose.\n- Used in AI models.\n\n> **Example:** PCA reducing image data size.\n\n---\n\n### Dimensionality Reduction in AI\n\n- Used in image processing.\n- Helps in data compression.\n- Improves model speed.\n- Reduces noise.\n- Enhances visualization.\n- Important ML technique.\n\n> **Example:** Face recognition using fewer features.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages\n\n- Faster processing.\n- Better visualization.\n- Less memory usage.\n- Improved accuracy.\n- Removes redundancy.\n- Simplifies datasets.\n\n> **Example:** Compressing large image datasets.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Image compression.\n- Genetic data analysis.\n- Financial modeling.\n- Recommendation systems.\n- Speech recognition.\n- AI training optimization.\n\n> **Example:** Google Photos grouping similar images.",
