    "title": "Model Training",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Model Training\n\n- Model training is teaching the ML model using data.\n- Algorithm learns patterns from data.\n- Uses training dataset.\n- Core step in ML workflow.\n- Improves prediction ability.\n- Done using algorithms.\n\n> **Example:** Training model to predict exam results.\n\n---\n\n### How Training Works\n\n- Input data is fed into model.\n- Model learns patterns.\n- Adjusts internal parameters.\n- Reduces errors gradually.\n- Repeats process many times.\n- Improves accuracy.\n\n> **Example:** Learning relationship between study hours and marks.\n\n---\n\n### Training Process Steps\n\n- Feed data into model.\n- Compare predicted vs actual output.\n- Calculate error.\n- Adjust model parameters.\n- Repeat process.\n- Improve performance.\n\n> **Example:** AI learning from past sales data.\n\n---\n\n### Algorithms Used in Training\n\n- Linear regression.\n- Decision trees.\n- Neural networks.\n- Support vector machines.\n- K-nearest neighbors.\n- Used based on problem type.\n\n> **Example:** Using decision tree for classification task.\n\n---\n\n### Importance of Training\n\n- Builds intelligent model.\n- Learns from data.\n- Improves prediction quality.\n- Core of machine learning.\n- Required for AI systems.\n- Ensures system intelligence.\n\n> **Example:** Training chatbot to understand questions.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Self-driving cars.\n- Fraud detection systems.\n- Recommendation engines.\n- Medical diagnosis systems.\n- Voice assistants.\n- AI chatbots.\n\n> **Example:** Training Netflix recommendation system.",
