    "id": "top-ai-6-2-2",
    "title": "Decision Trees",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Decision Trees\n\n- Decision Tree is a supervised learning algorithm.\n- Works like a flowchart structure.\n- Used for classification and regression.\n- Splits data into branches.\n- Easy to understand visually.\n- Very popular in AI.\n\n> **Example:** Deciding if a loan is approved or not.\n\n---\n\n### How Decision Trees Work\n\n- Data is split based on conditions.\n- Each node represents a decision.\n- Branches show outcomes.\n- Leaf nodes give final result.\n- Works step-by-step.\n- Simple logic-based model.\n\n> **Example:** If income > 50k → approve loan.\n\n---\n\n### Structure of Decision Tree\n\n- Root node (starting point).\n- Decision nodes (conditions).\n- Branches (possible outcomes).\n- Leaf nodes (final result).\n- Hierarchical structure.\n- Easy to interpret.\n\n> **Example:** Yes/No decision system for admission.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Decision Trees\n\n- Easy to understand.\n- No need for data scaling.\n- Works with numerical and categorical data.\n- Visual representation.\n- Fast predictions.\n- Useful in AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Medical diagnosis decision system.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations\n\n- Can overfit data.\n- Sensitive to small changes.\n- Complex trees become hard to manage.\n- Less accurate in some cases.\n- Needs pruning.\n- Can be unstable.\n\n> **Example:** Small data change leads to different tree.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Loan approval systems.\n- Medical diagnosis.\n- Fraud detection.\n- Customer classification.\n- Risk analysis.\n- Recommendation systems.\n\n> **Example:** Bank deciding credit approval.",
