    "id": "top-ai-6-3-1",
    "title": "Accuracy",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Accuracy\n\n- Accuracy measures how correct a model is.\n- It is the ratio of correct predictions to total predictions.\n- One of the simplest evaluation metrics.\n- Used in classification problems.\n- Helps measure model performance.\n- Important in AI evaluation.\n\n> **Example:** 90 correct predictions out of 100 = 90% accuracy.\n\n---\n\n### How Accuracy is Calculated\n\n- Accuracy = (Correct Predictions / Total Predictions) × 100.\n- Shows overall correctness.\n- Easy to understand metric.\n- Used for balanced datasets.\n- Common in ML models.\n- Helps compare models.\n\n> **Example:** 80 correct out of 100 = 80% accuracy.\n\n---\n\n### When Accuracy Works Well\n\n- Works best with balanced data.\n- Useful when classes are equal.\n- Simple evaluation method.\n- Common in basic ML tasks.\n- Easy to interpret.\n- Widely used metric.\n\n> **Example:** Equal number of spam and non-spam emails.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations of Accuracy\n\n- Misleading in imbalanced datasets.\n- Does not show error types.\n- Can hide poor performance.\n- Not enough alone.\n- Needs other metrics.\n- Limited insight.\n\n> **Example:** 95% accuracy but poor fraud detection.\n\n---\n\n### Accuracy in AI Systems\n\n- Used in classification models.\n- Helps evaluate predictions.\n- Common in ML workflows.\n- Important for model selection.\n- Used with other metrics.\n- Core evaluation tool.\n\n> **Example:** Spam filter accuracy check.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Email spam detection.\n- Image classification.\n- Medical diagnosis systems.\n- Voice recognition.\n- Fraud detection systems.\n- AI recommendation systems.\n\n> **Example:** Checking if email is spam or not.",
