    "id": "top-ai-7-1-1",
    "title": "Neural Networks Basics",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Neural Networks\n\n- Neural Networks are a core part of Deep Learning.\n- Inspired by how the human brain works.\n- Consist of connected units called neurons.\n- Learn patterns from large amounts of data.\n- Used for complex AI tasks.\n- Improve with training.\n\n> **Example:** Recognizing faces in photos like humans do.\n\n---\n\n### How Neural Networks Work\n\n- Data is passed through neurons.\n- Each connection has a weight.\n- Neurons process and pass signals.\n- Output is generated after processing.\n- Model learns by adjusting weights.\n- Improves with experience.\n\n> **Example:** AI recognizing handwritten digits.\n\n---\n\n### Artificial Neuron Concept\n\n- Takes input values.\n- Applies weights to inputs.\n- Adds bias value.\n- Uses activation function.\n- Produces output signal.\n- Basic building block of AI.\n\n> **Example:** Deciding if email is spam or not.\n\n---\n\n### Why Neural Networks are Important\n\n- Handle complex patterns.\n- Work well with images, text, and audio.\n- Learn automatically from data.\n- Better than traditional algorithms for deep data.\n- Used in modern AI systems.\n- Highly scalable models.\n\n> **Example:** Voice assistants understanding speech.\n\n---\n\n### Deep Learning Connection\n\n- Neural Networks power Deep Learning.\n- More layers = deeper learning.\n- Used for advanced AI tasks.\n- Learns hierarchical patterns.\n- Works with big data.\n- Core of modern AI.\n\n> **Example:** Self-driving cars detecting objects.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Image recognition systems.\n- Speech recognition.\n- Chatbots and AI assistants.\n- Medical diagnosis tools.\n- Translation systems.\n- Autonomous vehicles.\n\n> **Example:** Google Photos face recognition.",
