    "id": "top-ai-8-1-1",
    "title": "What is NLP?",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to NLP (Natural Language Processing)\n\n- NLP is a branch of Artificial Intelligence.\n- It helps computers understand human language.\n- Works with text and speech data.\n- Combines linguistics and machine learning.\n- Used in many AI applications.\n- Bridges human communication and machines.\n\n> **Example:** Chatbots like customer support assistants.\n\n---\n\n### How NLP Works\n\n- Takes human language as input.\n- Converts text into machine-readable format.\n- Analyzes grammar and meaning.\n- Extracts useful information.\n- Produces meaningful output.\n- Uses AI and ML models.\n\n> **Example:** Google Translate understanding sentences.\n\n---\n\n### Components of NLP\n\n- Syntax (structure of sentences).\n- Semantics (meaning of words).\n- Tokenization (splitting text).\n- Named Entity Recognition.\n- Sentiment analysis.\n- Speech processing.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting names in a sentence.\n\n---\n\n### Why NLP is Important\n\n- Enables human-computer communication.\n- Automates text analysis.\n- Improves user experience.\n- Used in search engines.\n- Powers chatbots and assistants.\n- Handles large text data.\n\n> **Example:** Siri understanding voice commands.\n\n---\n\n### Applications of NLP\n\n- Chatbots and virtual assistants.\n- Machine translation.\n- Sentiment analysis.\n- Voice recognition systems.\n- Text summarization.\n- Spam detection.\n\n> **Example:** Amazon Alexa answering questions.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life NLP Examples\n\n- Google Search engine.\n- WhatsApp predictive text.\n- Grammarly grammar correction.\n- YouTube subtitles.\n- Social media moderation.\n- Email spam filters.\n\n> **Example:** Autocomplete in mobile keyboards.",
