    "id": "top-ai-8-2-1",
    "title": "Chatbots",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Chatbots\n\n- Chatbots are AI systems that simulate conversation.\n- They use Natural Language Processing (NLP).\n- Can interact with users in text or voice form.\n- Provide instant responses to queries.\n- Used in customer service and support systems.\n- Work 24/7 without human effort.\n\n> **Example:** WhatsApp or website customer support bots.\n\n---\n\n### How Chatbots Work\n\n- User sends a message.\n- NLP processes the text.\n- AI understands intent of user.\n- System generates response.\n- Response is sent back to user.\n- Continuous interaction loop.\n\n> **Example:** Asking “What are your working hours?”\n\n---\n\n### Types of Chatbots\n\n- Rule-based chatbots.\n- AI-powered chatbots.\n- Voice-based chatbots.\n- Hybrid chatbots.\n- Each type has different complexity.\n- Used in different industries.\n\n> **Example:** Simple FAQ bot vs AI assistant like Siri.\n\n---\n\n### Benefits of Chatbots\n\n- Fast customer support.\n- Reduces human workload.\n- Available 24/7.\n- Handles multiple users at once.\n- Cost-effective solution.\n- Improves user experience.\n\n> **Example:** Online shopping support assistant.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations of Chatbots\n\n- May not understand complex queries.\n- Depends on training data.\n- Can give incorrect responses.\n- Limited emotional understanding.\n- Needs continuous updates.\n- Not fully human-like.\n\n> **Example:** Misunderstanding user complaint.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- E-commerce customer support.\n- Banking assistants.\n- Educational help bots.\n- Healthcare appointment systems.\n- Social media messaging bots.\n- AI assistants.\n\n> **Example:** Amazon chatbot helping with orders.",
