    "id": "top-ai-8-2-3",
    "title": "Sentiment Analysis",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Sentiment Analysis\n\n- Sentiment analysis is part of NLP.\n- It detects emotions in text.\n- Classifies text as positive, negative, or neutral.\n- Used in social media and reviews.\n- Helps understand user opinions.\n- Important in AI decision systems.\n\n> **Example:** Analyzing product reviews on Amazon.\n\n---\n\n### How Sentiment Analysis Works\n\n- Text is collected from users.\n- NLP processes the text.\n- AI detects emotional tone.\n- Classifies sentiment category.\n- Generates result.\n- Uses machine learning models.\n\n> **Example:** “This product is amazing” → Positive\n\n---\n\n### Types of Sentiment Analysis\n\n- Positive sentiment.\n- Negative sentiment.\n- Neutral sentiment.\n- Fine-grained sentiment (very positive, etc.).\n- Emotion detection (happy, sad, angry).\n- Used in advanced AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting angry customer feedback.\n\n---\n\n### Importance of Sentiment Analysis\n\n- Understands customer opinions.\n- Helps businesses improve products.\n- Analyzes social media trends.\n- Supports decision-making.\n- Useful in marketing.\n- Improves user experience.\n\n> **Example:** Analyzing Twitter opinions about a brand.\n\n---\n\n### Challenges in Sentiment Analysis\n\n- Sarcasm detection is difficult.\n- Language ambiguity.\n- Mixed emotions in text.\n- Context misunderstanding.\n- Requires large datasets.\n- Needs continuous improvement.\n\n> **Example:** “Great, just what I needed!” (sarcastic negative).\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Product review analysis.\n- Social media monitoring.\n- Brand reputation tracking.\n- Customer feedback systems.\n- Political opinion analysis.\n- Market research.\n\n> **Example:** Companies analyzing customer satisfaction online.",
