    "id": "top-ai-9-2-1",
    "title": "Face Recognition",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Face Recognition\n\n- Face recognition is a Computer Vision application.\n- It identifies or verifies a person from an image/video.\n- Uses AI and deep learning models.\n- Works by analyzing facial features.\n- Converts face into numerical data.\n- Used in security and authentication systems.\n\n> **Example:** Unlocking a smartphone using face ID.\n\n---\n\n### How Face Recognition Works\n\n- Camera captures face image.\n- Image is processed into pixels.\n- AI extracts facial features (eyes, nose, mouth).\n- Features are converted into a digital vector.\n- Compared with stored database faces.\n- Match gives identification result.\n\n> **Example:** Airport security scanning passengers.\n\n---\n\n### Key Techniques Used\n\n- Feature extraction.\n- Face detection.\n- Deep learning models (CNNs).\n- Image preprocessing.\n- Pattern matching algorithms.\n- Face encoding systems.\n\n> **Example:** Facebook tagging photos automatically.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Face Recognition\n\n- Fast and automated identification.\n- High security level.\n- No need for passwords.\n- Easy user authentication.\n- Used in real-time systems.\n- Reduces human effort.\n\n> **Example:** Mobile banking login using face scan.\n\n---\n\n### Challenges\n\n- Lighting conditions affect accuracy.\n- Changes in appearance (glasses, beard).\n- Privacy concerns.\n- Requires large datasets.\n- Can be fooled by similar faces.\n- Needs strong security.\n\n> **Example:** Failure to recognize face in low light.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Smartphone unlocking systems.\n- Airport security systems.\n- Attendance systems in schools.\n- Banking authentication.\n- Surveillance systems.\n- Social media tagging.\n\n> **Example:** CCTV identifying criminals.",
