    "title": "Object Detection",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Object Detection\n\n- Object detection identifies objects in images or videos.\n- Detects multiple objects at once.\n- Shows location using bounding boxes.\n- Uses Computer Vision and AI.\n- Important in real-world AI systems.\n- Works in real-time environments.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting cars and people in traffic cameras.\n\n---\n\n### How Object Detection Works\n\n- Image is taken as input.\n- AI scans image for objects.\n- Features are extracted.\n- Objects are classified.\n- Bounding boxes are drawn.\n- Output shows labeled objects.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting pedestrians on roads.\n\n---\n\n### Techniques Used\n\n- Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs).\n- YOLO (You Only Look Once).\n- R-CNN models.\n- Feature extraction methods.\n- Deep learning frameworks.\n- Real-time detection algorithms.\n\n> **Example:** Self-driving cars detecting obstacles.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Object Detection\n\n- Detects multiple objects at once.\n- Works in real-time.\n- Improves automation systems.\n- High accuracy with AI models.\n- Useful in safety systems.\n- Scalable technology.\n\n> **Example:** Traffic monitoring systems.\n\n---\n\n### Challenges\n\n- Complex backgrounds affect accuracy.\n- Requires large datasets.\n- High computational cost.\n- Difficult in low-quality images.\n- Needs powerful hardware.\n- Real-time processing challenges.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting objects in foggy weather.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Self-driving cars.\n- Security surveillance systems.\n- Retail product detection.\n- Medical imaging analysis.\n- Drone monitoring systems.\n- Robotics navigation.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting vehicles in parking systems.",
