    "title": "Image Classification",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Image Classification\n\n- Image classification assigns a label to an image.\n- Uses AI and deep learning models.\n- Works on single object recognition.\n- Converts image into category.\n- One of the basic CV tasks.\n- Very important in AI systems.\n\n> **Example:** Identifying whether image is cat or dog.\n\n---\n\n### How Image Classification Works\n\n- Image is input to AI model.\n- Pixels are analyzed.\n- Features are extracted.\n- Model predicts category.\n- Output label is assigned.\n- Uses trained neural networks.\n\n> **Example:** Classifying fruit images as apple or banana.\n\n---\n\n### Techniques Used\n\n- Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs).\n- Deep learning models.\n- Feature extraction methods.\n- Transfer learning.\n- Image preprocessing techniques.\n- Large labeled datasets.\n\n> **Example:** Google Photos sorting images.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages of Image Classification\n\n- Simple and effective.\n- High accuracy with deep learning.\n- Automates image sorting.\n- Saves time and effort.\n- Used in many industries.\n- Easy to implement.\n\n> **Example:** Sorting images into folders automatically.\n\n---\n\n### Challenges\n\n- Requires large labeled datasets.\n- Sensitive to image quality.\n- Can misclassify similar objects.\n- Needs strong computing power.\n- Limited in complex scenes.\n- Depends on training data quality.\n\n> **Example:** Confusing cat and fox images.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Medical image diagnosis.\n- Photo organization apps.\n- Security systems.\n- Wildlife classification.\n- Social media tagging.\n- Industrial quality control.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting diseases from X-ray images.",
