    "title": "NumPy",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to NumPy\n\n- NumPy is a Python library for numerical computing.\n- Used for working with arrays and matrices.\n- Provides fast mathematical operations.\n- Core tool in data science and AI.\n- Foundation for many ML libraries.\n- Very efficient and fast.\n\n> **Example:** Storing image pixels in arrays.\n\n---\n\n### Why NumPy is Used\n\n- Faster than normal Python lists.\n- Handles large datasets efficiently.\n- Supports multi-dimensional arrays.\n- Provides mathematical functions.\n- Used in scientific computing.\n- Essential for AI models.\n\n> **Example:** Calculating matrix operations in ML.\n\n---\n\n### NumPy Arrays\n\n- Main structure is ndarray.\n- Can be 1D, 2D, or multi-dimensional.\n- Stores same type of data.\n- Efficient memory usage.\n- Easy manipulation of data.\n- Used in ML preprocessing.\n\n> **Example:** Image stored as 2D pixel array.\n\n---\n\n### Basic Operations\n\n- Addition, subtraction, multiplication.\n- Matrix operations.\n- Statistical functions.\n- Reshaping arrays.\n- Indexing and slicing.\n- Mathematical transformations.\n\n> **Example:** Scaling dataset values.\n\n---\n\n### NumPy in AI\n\n- Used in deep learning frameworks.\n- Handles image and signal data.\n- Used in model computations.\n- Supports vector operations.\n- Improves performance.\n- Core AI tool.\n\n> **Example:** Processing image data for CNNs.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Image processing systems.\n- Machine learning models.\n- Scientific research.\n- Data analysis tools.\n- Financial modeling.\n- Engineering simulations.\n\n> **Example:** AI analyzing medical images.",
