    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Pandas\n\n- Pandas is a Python data analysis library.\n- Used for structured data handling.\n- Works with tables (dataframes).\n- Makes data easy to analyze.\n- Very popular in data science.\n- Essential for AI preprocessing.\n\n> **Example:** Student marks stored in table format.\n\n---\n\n### Why Pandas is Used\n\n- Easy data manipulation.\n- Handles large datasets.\n- Supports CSV, Excel files.\n- Clean and organize data.\n- Powerful analysis tools.\n- Used in AI pipelines.\n\n> **Example:** Reading Excel dataset for ML model.\n\n---\n\n### DataFrames in Pandas\n\n- Main data structure is DataFrame.\n- Works like a table (rows and columns).\n- Easy to filter and sort data.\n- Supports multiple data types.\n- Very flexible structure.\n- Core feature of Pandas.\n\n> **Example:** Student record table.\n\n---\n\n### Data Cleaning with Pandas\n\n- Remove missing values.\n- Fix incorrect data.\n- Filter rows and columns.\n- Handle duplicates.\n- Transform data formats.\n- Prepare data for ML.\n\n> **Example:** Cleaning customer dataset before training model.\n\n---\n\n### Pandas in AI\n\n- Used in data preprocessing.\n- Prepares data for ML models.\n- Works with NumPy and Scikit-learn.\n- Helps in feature engineering.\n- Essential for AI workflows.\n- Improves model accuracy.\n\n> **Example:** Preparing sales data for prediction.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Business analytics.\n- Financial data analysis.\n- Healthcare data processing.\n- E-commerce systems.\n- Research data handling.\n- AI model preparation.\n\n> **Example:** Analyzing customer purchase behavior.",
