    "id": "top-ai-12-2-2",
    "title": "Image Classifier",
    "duration": "15 mins",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "### Introduction to Image Classifier\n\n- Image classifier identifies objects in images.\n- Uses deep learning and computer vision.\n- Assigns labels to images.\n- Very popular AI beginner project.\n- Works with trained datasets.\n- Core part of AI vision systems.\n\n> **Example:** Identifying cat vs dog images.\n\n---\n\n### How It Works\n\n- Image is input into system.\n- Pixels are analyzed.\n- Features are extracted using CNN.\n- Model compares learned patterns.\n- Predicts category label.\n- Outputs result.\n\n> **Example:** Image → “Car” classification\n\n---\n\n### Key Techniques Used\n\n- Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs).\n- Image preprocessing.\n- Feature extraction.\n- Deep learning models.\n- Training with labeled images.\n- Transfer learning.\n\n> **Example:** Google Photos sorting images automatically.\n\n---\n\n### Advantages\n\n- High accuracy in classification.\n- Automates image labeling.\n- Saves time and effort.\n- Works with large datasets.\n- Used in many industries.\n- Scalable AI solution.\n\n> **Example:** Sorting photos into categories automatically.\n\n---\n\n### Limitations\n\n- Needs large dataset.\n- High computing power required.\n- Sensitive to image quality.\n- May misclassify similar objects.\n- Requires training time.\n- Complex model tuning.\n\n> **Example:** Confusing dog and wolf images.\n\n---\n\n### Real-Life Applications\n\n- Medical image diagnosis.\n- Face recognition systems.\n- Autonomous vehicles.\n- Security systems.\n- Wildlife classification.\n- E-commerce product tagging.\n\n> **Example:** Detecting diseases from X-ray images.",
